---
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro"
import Tile from "@components/Tile.astro"
import ImageTile from "@components/ImageTile.astro"
---

<PageLayout title="Story" description="Who I am, what I do, and what I like to build.">
  <Tile color="soft" size="lg">
    <h1 class="m-0 text-[clamp(40px,7vw,72px)] leading-[1.04]">Story</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[720px] text-[25px] leading-[1.45]">I help enterprise teams make promotions and loyalty work at scale. But mostly I'm a builder. If it needs hands, technique and a bit of patience, I'm in.</p>
  </Tile>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    <Tile color="paper" size="lg" class="space-y-4 text-[17px]">
      <p class="m-0">I'm Prash, born and brought up in India and now based in Munich, Germany. I work as a Principal Enterprise Sales Engineer at Talon.One.</p>
      <p class="m-0">I'm a builder. I get a stupid amount of joy out of putting things together. Lego, IKEA furniture, furniture I made myself, software. If it needs technique and my hands, I'm interested. I've also renovated my entire home: plastering the walls (that's <em>Verputz</em> for the Germans), painting, laying parkett flooring. Nobody asked me to. I just couldn't leave it alone.</p>
      <p class="m-0">I live by Naval Ravikant's idea: learn to build, learn to sell, and you're unstoppable. I'm decent at the first half. Building a business turns out to be a lot harder than assembling a bookshelf, and there's no instruction leaflet. So that's where I am right now, at a junction, figuring it out.</p>
    </Tile>
    <ImageTile
      class="min-h-[420px]"
      color="photo"
      src="/assets/prash.jpg"
      alt="Prash smiling in an orange cap and patterned shirt, with green hills and water behind him"
      position="50% 35%"
    />
  </div>
  <Tile color="sky" size="lg" class="space-y-4 text-[17px]">
    <h2 class="m-0 text-[clamp(28px,5vw,40px)] leading-[1.1]">How I got here</h2>
    <p class="m-0">I started as a developer at Bosch, writing C++ for car multimedia. For almost three years. Why did I even do that for that long? In fairness, we built infotainment for Suzuki, VW and Nissan, showed it at CES, and won an award at CES 2016 for reducing driver distraction. And Bosch was my first window into Germany, which is how I ended up here. So not a complete waste.</p>
    <p class="m-0">Then I did my Masters at TUM in computer vision, and spent almost the entire time in imposter syndrome. A short stint as a data scientist at Sixt followed, predicting the best way to de-fleet cars. After that I joined a start-up as a computer vision and ML engineer, working on SLAM and deep learning to turn point clouds into floor plans. Proper nerd stuff, and I loved it.</p>
    <p class="m-0">Somewhere along the way I realised I'm more than a code monkey. I'm a part-time extrovert, someone people pay to listen to talk, and sometimes also to pause and hear me speak. I always felt I could connect with people. A people's person? Maybe that's what pushed me into pre-sales, first at Twilio and now at Talon.One. Or, lol, maybe it was just my wife saying "you can do better".</p>
    <p class="m-0"><a href="/work" class="link">Where I've worked →</a></p>
  </Tile>
  <Tile color="paper" size="lg" class="space-y-4 text-[17px]">
    <p class="m-0">The other half of me is culture and history. Indian philosophy pulls me in every time. I think it's because that's where I find my identity. Far from India, you start digging.</p>
    <p class="m-0">And then there's the day job of being a middle-aged man trying to balance being a good husband, a great father and a good dog daddy. Some days I'm good at one of those. Never all three.</p>
    <p class="m-0">Maybe that's why the internet has been my first home since the early 2000s. It's where I can tinker, rant, build and write about all of it. So this is my story. Welcome to the rabbit hole.</p>
  </Tile>
</PageLayout>
